# BuildKit reads this file — named after the Dockerfile beside it — instead of
# the context root's .dockerignore. The context is the whole repository, so
# without it every node_modules tree and the entire .git history would be
# uploaded to the daemon to build a sample app.
#
# Everything is excluded, then the two directories the build actually reads are
# added back, minus their local build products (the image builds its own).
*
!packages/obstack-js
!demo/sdk-sample-ts
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/*.tgz
